    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="0244" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/5882: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in Costa
                        Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-07T21:00:00-04:00">April 7, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. Your 168 of March 31. You are authorized to discuss proposed agreement on
                    basis of 33 cents per pound f.o.b. Port Limón and Puntarenas. The Department
                    regrets that a price of 35 cents per pound is out of line with the price in
                    other countries.</p>
                <p>Department’s circular telegram of March 28<anchor n="4" xml:id="d263-f1"/> will
                    give you attitude of this Government with respect to making tires available. We
                    are making allocations of domestic rubber supplies to this country and to the
                    other American republics on a basis which is at least as favorable to civilian
                    uses in the other American republics as in this country. Moreover Costa Rica is
                    obtaining military supplies from this country under Lend-Lease
                        arrangements<anchor n="5" xml:id="d263-f2"/> which include various articles
                    of rubber equipment. It is hoped that this may be found acceptable by the Costa
                    Rican Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
